id: pm-jev-replay-ambiguity
title: Refuse ambiguous native model aliases before replay pinning
description: Share admission native inventory resolution with replay and prove conflict refusal before inspection or inference in both inventory orders.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: admission,"gh:unbraind/pm-jev#100",replay
created_at: "2026-11-06T11:08:45.561Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T15:27:22.505Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T11:10:31.245Z",codex-sol,"Plan: use one validated inventory resolver for direct admission and replay before pinning; retain loopback-only replay and verify all equivalent rows remain local decision models. Cover conflicting and identical digests in both inventory orders with real HTTP request counts."
  "2026-11-06T11:15:18.717Z",codex-sol,"Implementation and linked tests pass (5/5). Behavioral revert in a disposable package copy: replacing only createOllamaReplayAdapter with the main implementation makes the new ambiguity regression fail (0/1, missing expected rejection); restoring the fix passes (1/1). Both inventory orders refuse before inspection/inference; same-digest duplicates succeed and every matching row must remain local with decision capability."
  "2026-11-06T11:15:26.706Z",codex-sol,"Validation: build, build:test, lint, typecheck, docstring (49 files, 1130 declarations) and duplication (0 percent) pass. Strict tracker health passes with the existing managed-extension version-skew warning. Full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to PR CI as requested. No merge, release or model download. Items remain in progress for orchestrator verification; bot-review loop follows PR creation."
  "2026-11-06T13:38:42.167Z",codex-sol,"Review round 3: valid recovery-guidance finding. Replay forwards the shared ambiguity remedy, but cannot select native inventory rows by digest. Keep one resolver/refusal remedy for both paths and direct users to resolve conflicting installed aliases then retry an installed name. Strengthen the existing both-order replay regression to reject unsupported sha256-selection guidance; its corrected-inventory continuation proves the stated recovery succeeds. Direct admission keeps explicit verified-digest support."
  "2026-11-06T13:43:57.106Z",codex-sol,"Review round 3 results: focused reference/serialization tests pass 9/9; linked reference tests pass 5/5. Build, build:test, lint, typecheck, docstring and zero-duplication checks pass. Restoring only resolveOllamaInventoryModel to the pre-round-3 function makes the strengthened replay recovery regression fail 0/1 because its remedy recommends unsupported sha256 selection; restoring the shared remedy passes 1/1. The same regression reconciles the inventory and successfully replays both row orders, proving the advised recovery works. The repeated null-synthesis suggestion remains declined under the documented SDK JSON-omission contract."
  "2026-11-06T13:43:58.321Z",codex-sol,"Correction to the earlier health summary: ambient local strict health fails on the existing pinned-host/managed-extension skew tracked by pm-jev-v2la. Storage, integrity and append-only history checks pass. Strict health passes with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration, and in clean CI. Earlier wording that ambient strict health passed with a warning was incorrect; no dependency provisioning or pins changed."
  "2026-11-06T13:57:19.182Z",codex-sol,"CI follow-up to round 3: the runtime remedy and guide prose were updated, but the guide refusal table still quoted the old digest-selection advice. The existing admission-docs contract test caught the mismatch. Correct the table to the shared supported remedy and include admission-docs.test.ts in the targeted run; no runtime logic, dependency pin or threshold changes."
  "2026-11-06T13:58:36.268Z",codex-sol,"CI documentation follow-up passes 12/12 targeted tests across admission-reference, admission-serialization and admission-docs. The existing refusal-table/runtime contract test failed before the table correction in CI and now passes. Runtime and built artifacts are unchanged by this documentation-only follow-up. Regenerate changelog after release of this claim, then push for fresh exact-head CI; round 4 remains queued."
  "2026-11-06T15:18:38.136Z",codex-sol,"Review round 4: restore the documented unsupported-model recovery sentence for invalid native names, missing inventories and missing/invalid digests while retaining their specific guidance. Expand the existing guide contract test across those lookup paths. Also rebuild each duplicate-inventory negative case from clean rows, then repair only its intended defect and require adapter recovery; this exposes leaked flags if the old test setup is restored. Resolution and admission validation logic remain shared."
  "2026-11-06T15:27:21.067Z",codex-sol,"Review round 4 validation: targeted admission-reference, admission-serialization and admission-docs tests pass 12/12. Build, build:test, lint, typecheck, docstring and zero-duplication checks pass. Disposable proofs each fail 0/1 and restore to 1/1: restore the shared resolver function without the documented recovery; restore the leaky negative-test setup; independently remove remote_host, remote_model or decision-capability safeguards. Correcting only the intended field recovers adapter creation for every isolated case. Linked reference/docs tests pass 5/5 and 3/3. The repeated null-synthesis suggestion remains declined under the chosen JSON-omission contract and actual SDK wire evidence."
